{"SEI_owner_translation_acceptance":"pending","authority_effect":"none","cross_definition_review_findings":[{"accepted_map_refs":[],"finding_id":"SEI-CONSUMER-FINDING-001","issue":"C53 current admission binds the exact Definition and D25 source, while embedded candidate/prototype metadata and source posture remain unchanged. No current contract directly binds the invariant; current Schema/v1 binds generic Schema D56 only.","status":"unresolved"},{"accepted_map_refs":[],"finding_id":"SEI-CONSUMER-FINDING-002","issue":"Generic Definition validation and exact pure projections accept normative prose forbidding review, allowing unowned witness absence, inferring enforcement from references or granting authority from amendments. Shape and repeatable rendering do not enforce amendment semantics.","status":"unresolved"},{"accepted_map_refs":[],"finding_id":"SEI-CONSUMER-FINDING-003","issue":"Schema/v1 requires typed content references, owner and scope but no amendment, reason, before/after, compatibility, witness, owned residue or rollout/rollback tuple. Missing amendment fields cannot be repaired by assuming Schema content is a change record.","status":"unresolved"},{"accepted_map_refs":[],"finding_id":"SEI-CONSUMER-FINDING-004","issue":"Whole Schema fixtures accept opaque or uncomputed content digests, unresolved owners and check profiles, absent evidence and changed schema content/scope under one ID. Allowed relation components do not alone enforce the exact role combination; the bound validator was read only, not executed.","status":"unresolved"},{"accepted_map_refs":[],"finding_id":"SEI-CONSUMER-FINDING-005","issue":"The two primary consumer labels resolve to exact normalization registry entries and current Definitions for Governance Axis Independence and Schema. Embedded candidate posture does not replace current admission; semantic references do not identify a filesystem consumer or establish an operational map.","status":"unresolved"},{"accepted_map_refs":[],"findin